# Distortion - four curves and an asymmetry.
#
# `mode` is which curve: soft is a tanh and rounds the peaks, hard clips them
# flat, fold turns them back on themselves and goes somewhere no amplifier
# does, tube is soft with a knee. `bias` is the extra: it pushes the signal off
# centre before the curve, so the two halves of the wave are treated
# differently and even harmonics appear - which is the difference between a
# valve and a transistor, and the reason one is described as warm.
#
# Families: soft, hard, fold, tube.

machine fx.Distortion

patch Init family=soft

patch Warm family=soft
  # Barely there: enough to round the peaks and thicken the middle, and not
  # enough to hear as an effect. The setting that goes on things rather than
  # the one that is the point of them.
  drive          2.5
  tone           9000 Hz
  mix            0.55

patch Crunch family=soft
  # Where it starts being audible. The top rolled back, because a distortion
  # that keeps every harmonic it makes is a fizz rather than a crunch.
  drive          9
  tone           5000 Hz

patch Fuzz family=hard
  # Clipped flat and hard. Everything above the threshold is the same height,
  # so what comes out is closer to a square than to what went in, and the
  # dynamics of the source are gone on purpose.
  mode           #1
  drive          22
  tone           6500 Hz

patch Wall family=hard
  # The end of the range with the tone wide open: no dynamics, no top cut,
  # nothing left of the original but its rhythm.
  mode           #1
  drive          40
  tone           16000 Hz

patch Fold family=fold
  # The curve turns back on itself instead of flattening, so a peak that goes
  # further comes out *lower*. Nothing physical does this, which is why it
  # sounds like nothing physical - the harmonics it makes are not a series.
  mode           #2
  drive          7
  tone           8000 Hz

patch Shatter family=fold
  # Folding hard, where the wave crosses back on itself several times in one
  # cycle. A sine goes in and something with no fundamental left comes out.
  mode           #2
  drive          26
  tone           12000 Hz

patch Tube family=tube
  # The soft knee, driven where a valve would be working: the peaks compress
  # before they distort, so it gets louder and fatter before it gets dirty.
  mode           #3
  drive          11
  tone           7000 Hz
  bias           0.25

patch Asymmetric family=tube
  # Bias at its most, which makes the curve treat the two halves of the wave
  # differently and fills in the even harmonics - the octave rather than the
  # fifth. This is the control that is not on most distortion boxes.
  mode           #3
  drive          14
  tone           6000 Hz
  bias           0.85
  mix            0.8
